.TH CCOL_DYNMQ_ENABLE_SENDING 3 "2026-09-20" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_dynmq_enable_sending \- turn sends on again on a dynamic queue
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_dynmq_enable_sending(ccol_dynamic_queue *dq);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function clears the flag that ccol_dynmq_disable_sending() set. The
queue therefore accepts a send again and does not return
ccol_not_permitted. A new queue already has sends turned on. You need this
call only after a call turned sends off.

The function wakes every write-direction waiter on this queue. Such a
waiter is a ccol_select() call, a ccol_select_timed() call, or an
ccol_event_loop registration. A waiter that parked while sends were off
therefore sees that the queue is writable again.

The messages in the queue from before the change do not change. A turn off
and a turn on never drop anything.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
dq   Dynamic queue that gets sends turned on
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success       - The function turned sends on
ccol_invalid_args  - dq is NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
A new queue already has sends turned on.
The function is thread-safe.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_dynmq_disable_sending (3),
.BR ccol_dynmq_send_zc (3),
.BR ccol_dynmq_msg_count (3),
.BR ccol_circq_enable_sending (3)
